; ─── THE THIEF ARENA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; Deliberately a flat slab and nothing else. The experiment here is whether the
; money loop reads — get rich, get robbed, chase the thief down — so there is no
; geometry to confuse it with, and nothing for a probe to get wrong.
;
; 24 coins at 5 each is 120 in the level against an exit that wants 90. That
; margin is on purpose: even if a thief keeps everything it took, the level is
; still finishable. A thief is a container, not a sink — see coin_thief.gd — and
; this is the level-design half of that same rule.
[node name="ThiefArena" type="Node3D"]

